messages:
jess: Quickstart report: sample app crashes on Deno Deploy during onboarding flow. Error: `TypeError: globalThis.crypto is undefined` when sdk.createClient() runs.

jess: We import from a CDN: `import { createClient } from 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@redwood-inference/js-sdk@latest/dist/index.mjs'` — works locally (Node) but Deploy fails.

mike: Deno Deploy sometimes strips webcrypto. Short workaround: set globals before importing SDK. Example snippet: 
```js
if (!globalThis.crypto) {
  const { webcrypto } = await import('https://deno.land/std/crypto/mod.ts');
  globalThis.crypto = webcrypto;
}
```
Then import the SDK.

priya: Also saw Bun oddness: it has fetch but Headers can be frozen. Our SDK mutates headers for auth which breaks on Bun. Detect `Object.isFrozen(headers)` and clone before mutating.

andre: For typing friction in Deno, publish a small `deno.d.ts` and `globals.d.ts` shipped with the package. That avoids forcing users to edit tsconfig/deno.json. Example `globals.d.ts`: 
```ts
declare global { var crypto: Crypto; var fetch: typeof globalThis.fetch; }
export {};
```

mike: We should add a `dist/deno/index.mjs` entry that only uses Web APIs (no node: deps). Update package.json `exports` map to point `./dist/deno` for `import '.../deno'`. Also document required globals in quickstart.

priya: CI note: edge-bot flagged flaky tests in Bun for `auth/retry` suite (429 backoffs). We should make retry/backoff configurable and add Bun/Deno to test matrix. E.g. `createClient({ retry: { maxAttempts: 3, baseDelayMs: 150 } })`.

edge-bot: CI: flaky runs (last 4) on bun-runner. Filing flaky ticket: #INF-927.

jess: Thanks — I'll prototype the deno dist and a tiny prelude in the quickstart. Will paste a minimal repro if anything still fails. :pray:
